    <!-- ====================================================
         PROBLEMS WE HELP SOLVE
         ==================================================== -->
    <section class="problems-section section bg-white" aria-labelledby="problems-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label" data-reveal>PROBLEMS WE HELP SOLVE</div>
        <h2 id="problems-heading" data-reveal>Challenges Holding Your Factory Back</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" data-reveal>Most apparel factories face the same recurring problems. We have spent 30+ years diagnosing and solving exactly these challenges — on the shop floor.</p>

                                                <div class="problems-grid" data-reveal>
          
          <!-- Problem 1: Factory Planning -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">01</span>
            <h3>New Factory Planning Without an Integrated Blueprint</h3>
            <p>New projects are initiated without a robust business plan, benchmarking or an integrated operating blueprint covering product strategy, capacity, shifts, machinery, layout, technology, MMR, IE and efficiency assumptions—creating investment and execution risk.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 2: Underutilised Potential -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">02</span>
            <h3>Underutilised Factory Potential</h3>
            <p>The factory is not planned and configured to realise its full potential—limiting capacity utilisation, productivity, throughput and opportunities for future growth.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 3: Merged Process Flow & Bottlenecks (Boxes 3 & 4) -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">03</span>
            <h3>Poor Process Flow, Bottlenecks &amp; Unbalanced Capacity</h3>
            <p>Disconnected layouts, excessive material handling, and uneven capacity across cutting, sewing, and finishing create chronic bottlenecks, waiting time, high WIP accumulation, and lower overall throughput.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 4: Fabric Loss & Cutting Room Waste -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">04</span>
            <h3>Fabric Loss &amp; Cutting Room Waste</h3>
            <p>Fabric consumption above standard, cutting room inefficiency and avoidable material cost leakage on every order.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 5: Low Productivity & Weak IE Systems -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">05</span>
            <h3>Low Productivity &amp; Weak IE Systems</h3>
            <p>Poor production flow, high WIP accumulation and an undertrained or absent Industrial Engineering function.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 6: Quality Failures & Rework -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">06</span>
            <h3>Quality Failures &amp; Rework</h3>
            <p>Alteration rates above standard, buyer audit failures and rework consuming capacity that should be producing.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 7: Buyer & Customer Readiness -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">07</span>
            <h3>Buyer &amp; Customer Visit Readiness Gaps</h3>
            <p>Inconsistent workplace standards, weak visual management and unresolved process gaps affect customer visits, audit outcomes and buyer confidence.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 8: Technology Not Integrated -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">08</span>
            <h3>Technology Not Integrated With Operations</h3>
            <p>Technology investments — ERP, WMS, tracking systems — that are not integrated with actual factory processes and workflows.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Problem 9: Improvements That Don't Last -->
          <div class="problem-card">
            <span class="problem-card-number">09</span>
            <h3>Improvements That Don't Last</h3>
            <p>Consultants exit and improvements revert within weeks — because capability transfer and governance systems were not built in.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

